(Bug #79's nearest working neighbour, and the only order the manual ever
 writes: the declaration above the read. Every example in LANGUAGE.md's
 "Variables" section has this shape, and it is what the author who wrote
 the rejected program meant. Both scalar types the bug printed as 0 are
 checked here, so a fix that rejected too much would fail this first.)

a text called label is "hello".
Print label.

a number called count is 42.
Print count.

Print "{label} {count}".
